#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:1
msgid "Feature Name: `option_result_map_or_default`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:2
msgid "Start Date: 2021-07-14"
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:3
msgid ""
"RFC PR: [rust-lang/rfcs#3148](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3148)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:4
msgid ""
"Rust Issue: [rust-lang/rust#138099](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/"
"issues/138099)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:6
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:9
msgid ""
"`Option` has the methods `unwrap`, `unwrap_or`, `unwrap_or_else` and "
"`unwrap_or_default`. It similarly has `map`, `map_or`, `map_or_else`, "
"however `map_or_default` is missing. The exact same problem exists for "
"`Result`. This RFC is a proposal to add this method to `Option` and `Result`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:13
msgid "Motivation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:16
msgid ""
"As mentioned before, a user might reasonably expect this method to exist, "
"based on the existence of other `or_default` methods such as "
"`unwrap_or_default`. Furthermore, this is a very common usecase. Searching "
"for `map_or_else` in `.rs` files in the official Rust repository it is "
"incredibly common to see instances like these:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:27
msgid ""
"In fact, from a manual count at the time of writing, 25 out of the 57 "
"occurrences of `map_or_else` in the Rust codebase could have been replaced "
"with an equivalent call to `map_or_default`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:30
msgid "Reference-level explanation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:33
msgid "The following implementation would get added to `core::option::Option`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:46
msgid "The following implementation would get added to `core::result::Result`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:59
msgid "Drawbacks"
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:62
msgid ""
"It adds another method to `Option` and `Result`, which may be considered as "
"cluttered by some."
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:64
msgid "Rationale and alternatives"
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:67
msgid ""
"`.map_or_else(Default::default, ...)` can be written, although it is "
"significantly longer."
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:68
msgid ""
"In case `feature(default_free_fn)` stabilizes a user can write `."
"map_or_else(default, ...)` after `std::default::default`, which is a bit "
"shorter."
msgstr ""

#: src/3148-option-result-map-or-default.md:71
msgid ""
"However, neither alternative solves the discrepancy between "
"`unwrap_or_default` existing but `map_or_default` not existing."
msgstr ""

